# Version bump on ticket / feature completion

Source of truth: **`mobile/package.json`** `"version"`. Full policy: `docs/agents/versioning.md`.

**Never create, update, or restore a separate `VERSION` file** (repo root or elsewhere). If one exists, delete it and keep the version only in `mobile/package.json`.

## When to bump

Before the auto-commit that lands a completed **ticket** or **feature** (typically right after a **valid** `/code-review`):

1. If `mobile/package.json` is missing, skip the bump (and note that in the summary). Do **not** create a `VERSION` file as a substitute.
2. Otherwise read `"version"`, increment **PATCH** by 1 (`0.1.1` → `0.1.2`). Do not change MAJOR/MINOR unless the user asks.
3. Write the new value to `mobile/package.json` `"version"` only (no `v` prefix; keep JSON valid).
4. Stage `mobile/package.json` with the rest of the work and commit via `/commit`.
5. Put `Version: X.Y.Z` in the commit body and link the issue when known (`Closes #N` / `Refs #N`).

## When not to bump

- `mobile/package.json` does not exist yet — skip; never invent a `VERSION` file
- Publishing tickets with `/to-tickets` (creation only)
- Invalid code-review (no commit → no bump)
- Work that is not a ticket/feature deliverable
- Empty commits / clean tree after review with nothing to bump

If several tickets are completed in one commit, bump PATCH once per ticket completed in that commit (N tickets → +N), or ask the user if unsure.
